{"id": "EUVD-2026-99247", "enisaUuid": "d1c1e93e-ca11-3780-9c22-f306cfd2ae78", "description": "Roo Code through 3.54.0 contains a command approval bypass vulnerability in parseCommandLine() that allows attackers to auto-approve arbitrary shell commands by placing a command substitution in command position. Attackers using indirect prompt injection can submit commands like $(echo touch /tmp/x) that pass the echo allowlist check, causing the shell to execute the output without user approval.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:49:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T22:27:58", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/7rah/oss-cve/blob/6adb836d24ca446fd168c3acdc4c170beb77fe0f/roocode-group16-output-as-command.md", "https://github.com/RooCodeInc/Roo-Code/blob/v3.54.0/src/shared/parse-command.ts#L100-L172", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/roo-code-through-3.54.0-auto-approve-bypass-via-command-substitution-at-command-position"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110206", "GHSA-r2h8-r3xm-p2rm"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.47, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "44faf349-6f0b-3a85-bfb7-7b81784c3ffe", "product": {"name": "Roo-Code", "vendor": {"name": "RooCodeInc"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.54.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cc47d991-36e6-3e0d-9eac-68a8233e3cb5", "vendor": {"name": "RooCodeInc"}}], "isExploited": false}